<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">KwaZulu-Natal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">KwaZulu-Natal is a province on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, created in 1994 by merging the province of Natal with the KwaZulu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>. Its largest city is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durban">Durban</a> and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietermaritzburg">Pietermaritzburg</a>. The region was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>, became the British colony of Natal in the 19th century, and remains home to most of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>'s Zulu-speaking population.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal.jpg" alt="KwaZulu-Natal" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: South African Tourism from South Africa · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Beach,_Durban,_KwaZulu-Natal,_South_Africa_(20504187132).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
